 1	# gate-functions.sh: the shell functions of the gate's summary and of its ladder comparison.
 2	#
 3	#   gate_summary <log-dir> <out-file> [machine-label]
 4	#                         writes summary.txt: one row per suite from the plain-formatter files under
 5	#                         $FORTRESS_HOME/ProjectFortress/TEST-RESULTS/, then the BUILD and Total time
 6	#                         lines of <log-dir>/{compileAll,testFast,testSystem,testSpecData}.txt, then
 7	#                         "# machine " lines from machine.sh with the label (default "gate")
 8	#   gate_compare <last-landed-summary> <this-summary>
 9	#                         prints the red lines (RED, EMPTY, COUNT DOWN, SUITE GONE), exit 1 if any;
10	#                         the system-<i> rows are one suite split by sorted index, compared by their sum
11	#   last_landed_summary   prints the path of the newest landed summary.txt
12	#   ladder_filter <file>  masks the "Operation took" time of a ladder run's output
13	#   ladder_compare <baseline-dir> <now-dir>
14	#                         one DOWN, UP, NEW, MISSING or STDOUT line per ladder file that moved
15	#   mg_phases <microgpt-phase.md>
16	#                         one "component<TAB>phase" line per row of the microGPT phase table
17	#
18	# Source it from the tree's root, with FORTRESS_HOME set to that root, in the same Bash call that uses
19	# the functions, since each call starts a new shell:
20	#
21	#     source explorations/coordinator/tools/gate-functions.sh
22	#
23	# It defines the functions and runs nothing. The batch script's gate role
24	# (explorations/coordinator/climb-batch-workflow.js, steps 5 and 7) sources it, and so can any gate run
25	# by hand (the fortress-repo skill's gate.md). Until 2026-10-10 the functions were strings of the batch
26	# script, and the skill extracted them with node and awk (explorations/reviews/skills-agenda-audit.md,
27	# finding GA2).
